<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5435" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭvĭus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		bis-via, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>having two ways</i> or <i>passages</i> (rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cic.): fauces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 516</span></i>
			.—So, calles, <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 5,
				395</span></i>:  di, deae, <i>worshipped
				at cross-roads</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			2105</span></i>.—Hence, <i>substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭvĭi</span></b> 
			(sc. di), <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 389</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">2104</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭvĭum</span></b> ,
				i, n., <i>a place with
				two ways</i>, or <i>where two ways meet.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in bivio portae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 238</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad bivia consistere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					38, 45, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 28, 32, § 144</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Marc.
				11, 4</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: bivium nobis ad culturam dedit
			natura, experientiam et imitationem, <i>a twofold
			means</i> or <i>method</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 18, 7</span></i>.—Of <i>a twofold
				love</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 486</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
